---
import TextPage from '~/layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { CONTACT, BUSINESS_PENDING, ANALYTICS } from '~/config/site';

const path = '/privacy-policy/';
---

<TextPage
  title="Privacy Policy | Cone Sleeves UK"
  description="How Cone Sleeves UK handles the personal information you send through enquiry forms, email, telephone and WhatsApp."
  path={path}
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  standfirst="What happens to the information you send us, why we hold it, and how to ask us to delete it."
  updated="2026-08-13"
  crumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
>
  <h2>Who this policy covers</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to conesleeves.co.uk and to enquiries sent to us by form, email,
    telephone or WhatsApp.
  </p>
  {
    !BUSINESS_PENDING.legalName && (
      <p class="pending">
        <strong>Data controller details pending</strong>
        The registered company name, company number and registered address of the data
        controller have not been published because they have not yet been supplied for this
        site. They must be added before launch — a privacy policy that does not identify
        the controller is incomplete. Nothing has been invented in their place.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only what you choose to send us. Through the enquiry forms that is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name.</li>
    <li>Your email address.</li>
    <li>Your telephone number, if you provide one.</li>
    <li>Your business name, if you provide one.</li>
    <li>The product, quantity and any message or specification you describe.</li>
    <li>Any artwork file you attach.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our web server also records the IP address a submission came from, for the short
    period needed to apply a rate limit that keeps automated spam off the form.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
  <p>
    To answer your enquiry, produce a quotation, and — if you place an order — to fulfil
    it. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in responding to a business enquiry you
    have initiated, and, once an order is placed, performance of a contract with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not use enquiry details for marketing unless you separately ask us to, and we do
    not sell or share them with third parties for their own purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not lead to an order are kept while there is a realistic prospect of
    the conversation continuing, and are deleted after that. Records relating to an actual
    order are kept for as long as we are required to retain business and tax records.
    Artwork files are kept while your job is live and while a reorder from the same die is
    plausible.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes it</h2>
  <p>
    Your enquiry is delivered to us by an email service provider and is stored in our email
    system. The website is hosted by a hosting provider that processes requests to it.
    These providers act on our instructions.
  </p>
  <p class="pending">
    <strong>Processor names pending</strong>
    The specific hosting, email and any customer-management providers used for the live
    site should be named here before launch, so this policy describes the actual
    arrangement rather than a generic one.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  {
    ANALYTICS.ga4 || ANALYTICS.gtm ? (
      <p>
        This site loads an analytics tag. See our <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>{' '}
        for what it sets and how to control it.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        This site currently sets no cookies of its own and loads no analytics or advertising
        scripts. If analytics is enabled later, our{' '}
        <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a> will describe exactly what it sets, and a
        consent mechanism will be added first.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>
    The WhatsApp buttons on this site open WhatsApp with a message addressed to us. Once
    you send it, the conversation is handled inside WhatsApp and is also subject to
    WhatsApp's own privacy terms, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK data protection law you can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold
    about you, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete it, or object to our processing of
    it. Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> and we will respond
    within one month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Information
    Commissioner's Office, the UK supervisory authority for data protection.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of this page. Material
    changes affecting how we handle existing enquiries will be notified directly to anyone
    affected.
  </p>
</TextPage>
